   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the private housing finance law, in relation to loans for state-aided limited-profit housing companies",
    "basePrintNo": "S5877",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5877-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §22-b, Priv Hous Fin L",
    "lawSection": "Private Housing Finance Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5877\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the private housing finance law, in relation to loans\nfor state-aided limited-profit housing companies\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nThe purpose of this bill is to allow Starrett City to refinance in\nexcess of its actual project cost in return for thirty years of\nadditional compliance with the provisions of the Mitchell-Lama\nprogram.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nThis bill would approve a loan and encumbrance in excess of the actual\nproject cost of a Mitchell-Lama project containing over five thousand\nrental units provided that:\n\n* rents paid by tenants may not be increased to pay for any subsequent\ndebt produced by the project;\n\n* the company enters into agreement to remain subject to the\nprovisions of article 2 of the private housing finance law for a\nperiod of no less than thirty years, from the issuance of the loan and\nencumbrance;\n\n* the greater of25 percent of the loan proceeds in excess of actual\nproject cost or $40 million of the loan proceeds go towards capital\nimprovements of existing structures and facilities;\n\n* the company creates a plan of all the capital improvements within\none year of the approval of the loan;\n\n* the company obligates the funds dedicated to capital improvements\nwithin three years;\n\n* the company submits the one-year plan and a report detailing the\nobligation of funds' to the governor, the Department of Housing and\nCommunity Renewal, the Assembly and the Senate; and\n\n* bi-monthly meeting are held between elected officials and the\nmembers of the project's residents' association until all money\nset-aside for the capital improvements is spent.\n\n EFFECTS OF PRESENT LAW WHICH THIS BILL WOULD ALTER :\nThis act amends the private housing finance law by adding a new\nSection 22-b.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThis legislation is meant to help refinance Starrett City and entice\nowners to stay in the Mitchell-Lama program for another thirty years.\nRecently, many owners in affordable housing communities have\nbought-out of the program, leaving tenants in a situation where their\nrent will increase to market price, which could be up to three times\nas much as their existing rent. The new money will give owners\nincentive to stay in the program.\n\nAlso, at least $40 million and possibly more depending on the size of\nthe loan will be set aside for capital improvements to individual\nhousing units and the important community areas, such as the power\nplant, garage or recreational facility. Tenants will have more rights,\nas bi-monthly meetings with owners and elected officials will allow\nfor their input on more issues.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nThis is new legislation.\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS :\nNone to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
